docs/sol/sol_round5.out-104-  existing DB. The doc's "already built and regression-tested" claim must be removed
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-105-  until the live record is migrated and re-attacked. The one job marked "shipped" has
docs/sol/sol_round5.out:106:  no run id, branch, or exact version attached.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-107-- Reviews are not yet bound to the exact code version merged (the known flaw, still
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-108-  open in the build).
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-109-
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-110-## Benchmark judgment (honest version to adopt)
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-111-
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-112-Safer than terminal use for: the Mac, credentials, production access, spend.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-113-More dangerous than terminal use for: unwanted repository changes and routine spend at
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-114-scale, unattended. Proportionate if stated and accepted that way.
--
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-148-    19	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-149-    20	## OWNER DECISION D (2026-07-17) — the proportionality reset
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-150-    21	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-151-    22	**The benchmark, stated the honest way (Sol round 7):** compared to the owner running
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-152-    23	Claude Code in his terminal today, this harness is **safer in blast radius** — the VM,
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-153-    24	credential absence, and hard caps protect the Mac, the secrets, production, and the
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-154-    25	wallet better than a bare terminal does — and **more autonomous**: it runs unattended,
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-155-    26	takes voice-triggered work, operates at overnight scale, and reads more injectable
docs/sol/sol_round5.out:156:    27	content than a supervised session. The extra autonomy risk lands almost entirely on
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-157-    28	*unwanted-but-source-reversible repository changes and routine spend*, and the owner
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-158-    29	accepts that explicitly (Decision E). It is a *development* harness. It is not, and
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-159-    30	does not claim to be, an autonomous production-release authority.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-160-    31	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-161-    32	Concretely:
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-162-    33	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-163-    34	- **"Ship" means landing code on the owner's own repos** — the thing git makes
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-164-    35	  reversible, and the thing agents already do from his terminal daily. After the
--
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-204-    75	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-205-    76	---
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-206-    77	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-207-    78	## The one-sentence shape
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-208-    79	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-209-    80	**OpenClaw drives the car. Agents work in a sealed workspace with no keys, everything
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-210-    81	they do is recorded and reviewed, work lands on the owner's repos like it does from his
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-211-    82	terminal — and the few genuinely irreversible things (history rewrite, production
docs/sol/sol_round5.out:212:    83	deploys, real money, patient data) sit behind doors no agent can open.**
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-213-    84	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-214-    85	---
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-215-    86	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-216-    87	## The threat model
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-217-    88	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-218-    89	Not the owner. The real threats, in order:
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-219-    90	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-220-    91	1. **An agent doing something nobody asked for.**
--
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1267-   442	  overrides: `autoreview --reviewers codex,claude --model codex=gpt-5.6-sol --thinking codex=high`.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1268-   443	  That is most of §6, for free.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1269-   444	- **Tailnet + launchd** = Gateway binds loopback:18789, **auto-configures Tailscale Serve**,
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1270-   445	  serves the Control UI on the same port; `openclaw gateway install` writes the launchd service.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1271-   446	  §2's networking and daemon requirements are shipped features.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1272-   447	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1273-   448	**Version pinning is not optional.** Three breaking releases in under 90 days in Q1 2026
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1274-   449	(2026.3.2, 2026.3.8, 2026.3.13). Exact pins are honored and not overwritten by the updater.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out:1275:   450	This is precisely the vendor-drift risk §9 names — pin an exact version, upgrade deliberately.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1276-   451	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1277-   452	### The voice server half is already built
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1278-   453	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1279-   454	**`kwindla/macos-local-voice-agents`** — reference implementation by Pipecat's originator
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1280-   455	(Kwindla Kramer, Daily CEO). Stack: Silero VAD · smart-turn v2 · **MLX Whisper · Kokoro TTS** ·
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1281-   456	WebRTC · React client. Claims **<800ms voice-to-voice on M-series** *with a local LLM in the loop*.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1282-   457	Our budget is 1.5s to first audio with the orchestrator doing the thinking — real headroom.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1283-   458	⚠️ Only 17 commits and **LICENSE unverified — check before forking.** Treat as demo-grade code
--
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1405-   576	re-architecture**. OpenClaw's provider abstraction gives us this nearly for free. Cheap insurance
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1406-   577	against being the next OpenClaw headline.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1407-   578	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1408-   579	---
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1409-   580	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1410-   581	## 6. Ranked recommendations
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1411-   582	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1412-   583	**Adopt as-is**
docs/sol/sol_round5.out:1413:   584	- OpenClaw core, **pinned to an exact version** — seats as `agents.list[]`, `codex` plugin for the
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1414-   585	  orchestrator, `agentRuntime.id: "claude-cli"` for the Claude seat.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1415-   586	- Native subagents for dispatch (`maxSpawnDepth: 2`, per-spawn `model` override).
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1416-   587	- `autoreview` skill as the gauntlet spine.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1417-   588	- `openclaw gateway install` (launchd) + Tailscale Serve auto-config.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1418-   589	- **Pipecat** (BSD-2) as the voice framework; `kokoro-onnx` via `pipecat-ai[kokoro]` for TTS;
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1419-   590	  `WhisperSTTServiceMLX` for STT.
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1420-   591	
docs/sol/sol_round5.out-1421-   592	**Fork / vendor**
